    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.36</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:06:24 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22336</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.36</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Updating while agents work is safe and says so: the update row tells you your chats keep working, Install asks first only if a terminal tab is running something (Install when free, Install now, Cancel), and drafts are kept across the restart.</li><li>The agent engine catches up on its own: an engine update that had to wait for running chats now installs as soon as they finish, or right away with Restart now.</li><li>The window controls sit in line with the duck in a normal window, as they do in full screen.</li><li>Squeak no longer ships Anthropic's agent kit inside the app: it downloads the exact published version from npm the first time it's needed and checks it before use.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.35</h4><ul><li>Conductor chats are marked with a plain connection symbol instead of Conductor's own app icon.</li><li>The licences of everything Squeak bundles (Node.js, its database driver, the agent SDK and more) are listed in full in the app's notices.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.34</h4><ul><li>Full screen: the window controls stay in while you move down from the menu bar to click them; they follow where the row really is instead of a fixed guess.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
